  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-16T18:03:56.173Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the most recent release(2018.3.3) of VRChat, more emojis were added to the list and replaced the old ones. The addition of more is definitely welcomed, but the change in style from minimalist to a more skeuomorphism-like design(very heavily inspired by Apple it seems as well, who still think that style can make a comeback). This change in style to the emoji set clashes with the new changes to the UI, which have added a more flat style to the quick menu and to the safety feature menu. And judging by some other changes, such as the world author window and the new loading image on thumbnails, both of which have been added in this update, VRChat seems to be pushing for a more modern design, instead of one that looks like it's being held back ten years in the past.  \n\nPersonally I've been enjoying the new changes and would hate to see those changes soured by poor and outdated design decisions.",
